  "limitations": [
    "Incremental findings compare a fresh frozen COPY + GET-encoding version with the spool candidate. Overview graphs compare cumulative stages with the original baseline.",
    "Only the POST outgoing buffer changes. Original benchmark/Makefile, GET, DB COPY, schema, session caching and client lifetimes remain unchanged.",
    "The main benchmark graph adds the first completed final after report; paired findings aggregate all three reports per version, not that single graph point.",
    "One MiB is the spool rollover threshold, not a total request-memory limit. One run and its encoded field can be larger; raw body, parsed models and field serialization remain in RAM.",
    "Temporary-file writes and SDK file reads are synchronous here. Disk capacity, page-cache use and concurrent disk contention need production evaluation.",
    "Small serial local samples do not establish production p95 or concurrent throughput. Do not attribute small GET timing shifts to this POST-only change.",
    "POST 50 has a worse median but a slightly lower mean and overlapping suite ranges. The data does not establish a uniform POST 50 latency regression or improvement.",
    "Original benchmarks regenerate random ASCII strings and UUIDs with the same structure and byte lengths; they are not byte-identical across suites. Cold CPU fixtures are fixed and matched before/after.",
    "Failed-upload file cleanup is tested; cleanup of an S3 object after later DB failure remains an existing cross-store limitation.",
    "The experiment implementation is preserved in commit 0def488 and reverted in a follow-up commit. Application SHA and source snapshots identify the measured experimental code; these measurements do not describe the restored current implementation. No push was made."
  ],
